         path data unchanged, and the F1 prefix selects the nonzero fill rule
         SVG uses, where WPF would otherwise default to even-odd and punch out
         the enclosed areas of letters like o and e. The artwork is 15 separate
         paths, which concatenate into one geometry as subpaths — no transforms,
         fills or clipping in the source to fold in first.

         Original viewBox 138.82 x 36.5, so the mark is wide — size it by
         height and let the width follow. The geometry fills that box exactly,
         which matters because a Viewbox scales the geometry's own bounds rather
         than the viewBox: padding in the artwork would quietly change how big
         the mark draws. -->
